enchilada: ADSP: boot the LPASS Q6 through SCM PAS and talk APR to it in gated stages (adsp=1..3, audio round 1)

Audio on this phone runs through the ADSP: the Q6 AFE drives QUAT MI2S to the speaker amp (MAX98927
at 0x3a on QUP SE4 per board overlay 17819/22; not a TFA98xx) and SLIMbus to the WCD9340, and the
apps talk to it in APR over GLINK. logs/audio/plan.md has the whole chain; this is its first part,
in a new bsd/dev/sweet_adsp.c, one attempt per boot, polled from its own thread, every stage a
prefix of the next ending in one "SWEET ADSP: stage N: ok/FAILED: ..." line, any failure running
the stop path (SMP2P stop request if it ran, SCM PAS shutdown, load_state adsp off).
1: read-only probe: the adsp region (enchilada2.dtb pil_adsp_mem 0x8c500000 + 0x1a00000) against
the kernel's RAM, SMEM v12 header + ptable, the apps<->adsp partition (hosts 0/2) and items 423
(global), 429, 443, 478, 479, 480, GCC's audio TBU GDSC vote. LPASS itself is not read.
2: adsp.mdt + adsp.b02..b13 from modem_a (UFS LUN 4) at the offsets of tools/mss-fw-table.py --adsp,
every crc32 checked before anything else; the mdt checked as qcom_mdt_pas_init would (header + hash
= the whole 7452-byte mdt, relocatable, extent 0x1a00000 = the region). Then Linux v6.12
qcom_q6v5_pas.c adsp_start for sdm845_adsp_resource_init: SMP2P item 429 ("master-kernel"), QMP
load_state adsp on, cx at its top corner (downstream's vdd_cx TURBO proxy vote), PAS id 1
init_image with the metadata in its own page (0xa1090000, unmapped before the call), mem_setup,
segments into the region (tails zeroed, windows dropped before auth), auth_and_reset, and SMP2P
item 443 "slave-kernel" ready (bit 1) within 5 s.
3: GLINK over SMEM to the ADSP (items 478/479/480 of partition 0/2, APCS IPC bit 8), every channel
the ADSP opens logged, "apr_audio_svc" and "IPCRTR" opened both ways with 8 intents each; APR from
APPS (5) to q6core (svc 3, ADSP 4): AVCS_CMD_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE every 100 ms until ready (3 s),
then AVCS_CMD_GET_FWK_VERSION (AVCS_GET_VERSIONS if unsupported), framework and service versions
logged; QRTR HELLO and the ADSP's NEW_SERVERs logged (nothing served yet); then a 30 s watch for a
fatal (crash reason item 423) and the stop path.
sweet_mss.c shares three things with the new thread: mss_scm() (no longer static), sweet_mss_qmp()
(the AOSS mailbox opened once and used under a lock; MSS's own load_state messages go through it)
and sweet_mss_smem_lock() (TCSR mutex 3 holds one value per processor, so the two apps threads
allocating SMEM items also need a lock). sweet_adsp_probe() runs right after sweet_mss_probe().
Host-checked against a fake SMEM/SCM/ADSP peer with the real modem_a.img (stages 1-3 and the
fail-closed path); not yet built in CI or booted.

